items. Searches for rename, Walls, scene, dialog and label found nothing this change closes. #389, #390 and #391, cited by the plan and change-log as follow-ups, all resolve as open, so C-B4 does not fire. C-B3: curation-ui's open items are #389 and #390, which are later plans of this series, and #94, which is not touched. No hygiene step is owed.", "fid": "R-15"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "note", "title": "Records Pass: older pending operator-verification steps send the operator to controls this change removed", "recommendation": "Covered set: all seven files_oracle records. The other six (api-contract.md, build-plan-ui-pass-walls.md, design-direction.md, ia-proposal.md, information-architecture.md, change-log.md) clear no bar. Their claims match the code: rename trims, refuses an empty or taken name with 400, republishes nothing, and answers the wall; the IA Walls rows describe the built card and dialog. In operator-verification.md, three entries still under ## Pending name controls this change removed: 'Walls \u203a a wall \u203a How it is set up \u203a Mat' (line 318), '*How \u2026 set up* and find *Shapes it shows*' (line 260), and '*Change* looks like a button beside *Skip*' (line 146). An operator working the pending list would look for a disclosure that no longer exists. This is NOTE, not WARNING, because operator-verification is bookkeeping exempt from Goal 4 drift. Fix it cheaply in the next commit: add one line to the new 'Walls, rebuilt to the page rules' entry saying those steps' controls are now in the card's Edit\u2026 dialog and Hanging picker. Scope: instance.", "files": [".prawduct/operator-verification.md"], "fid": "R-16"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 5, "note": 11}, "observations": [], "duration_seconds": 720, "scope": "ui-pass-walls", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_review